<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian three-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian three-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills fell to 10.199 percent from 10.255 percent at the previous auction on October 31.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Feb 6, 1997 (Jan 30, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.199 percent (10.255)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 642.225 million (955.225 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1.081 billion (893.1 billion)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 10.002-10.217 percent (10.150-10.263)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 10.002-10.301 percent (10.150-10.399)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 97 (72)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 222 (79)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
